  "note": "First election of the rural district council (four district electoral divisions, two councillors each), polled 6 April 1899. At the first meeting Maynard Sinton and William Adams were co-opted and three additional councillors chosen (Banbridge Chronicle, 19 April 1899, p. 3); they are not filed. Polled 6 April 1899; the Banbridge Chronicle and the Northern Whig (15 April 1899, p. 6) give the elected and not elected only, without figures or labels. Samuel Raivey was also nominated."
